{"title":"AI Use Policy","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"AI Use Policy"},"headingText":"Default rule","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\nAI use is generally permitted and often required in DSA261 because learning how to use AI well is part of the course.\n\nPermission to use AI does **not** transfer responsibility to AI.\n\n## What you must be able to show\n\nFor assessed TRACE work, you may be asked to document:\n\n- the prompt or query you used;\n- how the prompt/query changed;\n- what the AI contributed;\n- what you rejected or corrected;\n- what external evidence you used;\n- what decision remained yours.\n\n## Verification rule\n\n> **An LLM answer, citation, summary, or confidence statement is not independent verification evidence.**\n\nVerification must leave the model and reach an appropriate external source, dataset, document, or other independently inspectable evidence.\n\n## Disclosure\n\nWhen a Task asks for AI-use disclosure, report the actual use. Productive, transparent AI use is not penalised. Unverifiable or falsely represented process evidence may be.\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n## Default rule\n\nAI use is generally permitted and often required in DSA261 because learning how to use AI well is part of the course.\n\nPermission to use AI does **not** transfer responsibility to AI.\n\n## What you must be able to show\n\nFor assessed TRACE work, you may be asked to document:\n\n- the prompt or query you used;\n- how the prompt/query changed;\n- what the AI contributed;\n- what you rejected or corrected;\n- what external evidence you used;\n- what decision remained yours.\n\n## Verification rule\n\n> **An LLM answer, citation, summary, or confidence statement is not independent verification evidence.**\n\nVerification must leave the model and reach an appropriate external source, dataset, document, or other independently inspectable evidence.\n\n## Disclosure\n\nWhen a Task asks for AI-use disclosure, report the actual use. Productive, transparent AI 